PADL default pad [    hi]
PADL a custom pad character [****hi]
PADC default pad [  hi  ]
PADC a custom pad character [--hi---]
SUBSTRC to the end World
SUBSTRC with a length Wor
STRTRAN default replaces every one X two X two X two
STRTRAN with no replacement removes it [ two  two  two]
STRTRAN from the 2nd occurrence onward one two X two X two
STRTRAN one occurrence starting at the 2nd one two X two one two
STRTRAN flag 1 is case-insensitive, exact replacement x TWO x
STRTRAN flag 3 case-adjusts what flag 1 found X two X

STRTRAN nStartOccurrence 0         11

STRTRAN nNumberOfOccurrences 0         11
STREXTRACT plain hello
STREXTRACT the 3rd occurrence of the begin delimiter b
STREXTRACT flag 1 is case-insensitive delimiters hi
STREXTRACT flag 2 is the missing end delimiter hello
STREXTRACT flag 4 keeps the delimiters <a>hello</a>
STREXTRACT with no end delimiter at all reads to the end hello</a><b>world</b>
STRCONV uppercase, plain HELLO
STRCONV uppercase, with a locale HELLO
STRCONV uppercase, with a locale and its type HELLO
TEXTMERGE not recursive leaves the merged text alone value is <<1+1>>
TEXTMERGE recursive evaluates the merged text too value is 2
TEXTMERGE a left delimiter alone keeps >> on the right value is 2
TEXTMERGE both delimiters given value is 2
MLINE row 1 from its own start one two three four five
MLINE row 1 skipping five characters wo three four five
MLINE row 1 to exactly its own end is empty []
MLINE row 1 one past its own end lands on row 2 whole second line here
MLINE row 2 with an offset that has not reached it yet is row 2 whole second line here
